  "description": "IVEWEM crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C102 H124 Co2 Dy10 N12 O58 S2 2+,2(C4 H2 Co1 N4 O1 S4 1-),2(C2 H3 N1),2(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Dy1 (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Dy2 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy3 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy4 (Dy) has 9 O neighbors; Dy5 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Co1 (Co) has 3 O neighbors; Dy1A (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Dy2A (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy3A (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy4A (Dy) has 9 O neighbors; Dy5A (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Co1A (Co) has 3 O neighbors; Co2 (Co) has 1 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 16 pairs, 2 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.449-4.088 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 103.69-110.80°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Dy10Co2(L)4(OAc)16(SCN)2(CH3CN)2(H2O)4(OH)2(μ3-OH)4]·2Co(SCN)4H2O·2CH3CN·2H2O. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 16 OAc (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 4 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 2 OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 4 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
